Description: Workspaces of their own on every output, added by the user
 Labwc has one list of workspaces, and a workspace covers all outputs:
 switching it switches every monitor. On two monitors that means the side
 monitor cannot keep its windows while the main one changes workspace. This
 patch adds two options, both off by default, so stock behaviour is kept:
 .
 <desktops perOutput="yes">: every output in the layout gets a group of
 workspaces of its own, which is also its workspace group in
 ext-workspace-v1, so panels show the workspaces of the monitor they are
 on. GoToDesktop switches the output nearest to the cursor, SendToDesktop
 counts from the window's workspace. A window whose output changes (moved
 by hand or by MoveToOutput, placed by a window rule) goes to the current
 workspace of its new output. When an output leaves the layout, its windows
 are parked, keeping their workspace position, in a global group that is
 not announced to clients, and Labwc's evacuation then moves them to the
 same position on the output they land on.
 .
 <desktops dynamic="yes">: the user adds and removes workspaces while
 Labwc runs, as on macOS: with the new AddDesktop and RemoveDesktop actions,
 with GoToDesktop or SendToDesktop to="right" from the last workspace unless
 it is empty, and through ext-workspace-v1 (create_workspace and remove), so
 a panel can offer "+" and "x". A workspace stays while empty, workspaces do
 not wrap, and they are named by their position. A removed workspace hands
 its windows to its left neighbour (the right one for the first workspace);
 the last workspace of a group stays.
 .
 Inside, struct workspace_group holds what server.workspaces held (the list,
 current, last and the ext-workspace group). Without perOutput there is one
 global group spanning all outputs, which is Labwc's behaviour. The debug
 scene dump names per-output workspaces "OUTPUT/name".
 .
 Known limits: changing either option takes effect after a restart; the
 window menus list the workspaces of the output under the cursor.
 .
 Requested upstream in labwc/labwc issue 932; not forwarded yet.
Author: The Dodobian authors
Origin: vendor, https://github.com/dodobian/dodobian/tree/main/labwc
Forwarded: no
