diff --git a/docs/labwc-config.5.scd b/docs/labwc-config.5.scd
index 80930b3..391ce5c 100644
--- a/docs/labwc-config.5.scd
+++ b/docs/labwc-config.5.scd
@@ -626,6 +626,27 @@ extending outward from the snapped edge.
 *<desktops><prefix>*
 	Set the prefix to use when using "number" above. Default is "Workspace".
 
+*<desktops perOutput="">* [yes|no]
+	Give every output workspaces of its own. GoToDesktop switches the
+	workspaces of the output nearest to the cursor and leaves the other
+	outputs alone; SendToDesktop counts from the window's workspace. A
+	window moved to another output goes to that output's current
+	workspace. When an output leaves the layout, its windows move to
+	another output, to the workspace with the same position; clients of
+	ext-workspace-v1 see one workspace group per output. Every output
+	starts with the workspaces defined above. Default is no: a workspace
+	covers all outputs. Changing it takes effect after a restart.
+
+*<desktops dynamic="">* [yes|no]
+	Let the user add and remove workspaces while labwc runs, as on macOS:
+	with the AddDesktop and RemoveDesktop actions, with GoToDesktop or
+	SendToDesktop to="right" from the last workspace, and through
+	ext-workspace-v1 (create_workspace and remove). A workspace stays
+	while empty, until it is removed. Workspaces start as defined above
+	and are named by their position, from <names> and then with the
+	prefix. With perOutput, every output has its own. Default is no.
+	Changing it takes effect after a restart.
+
 ## THEME
 
 *<theme><name>*
